c A hand-written UNSAT instance on which the implication graph learns the unit x3 = 0 and the
c refutation needs it. Solve with --bve=false --implication-graph-min-new-clauses=0.
c With the unit x2 = 1, the three width-2 clauses say that x3 = 1 implies x4 = 1, x5 = 1 and
c x4 + x5 = 1, whose sum is 0 = 1, so x3 = 0. Root propagation reaches nothing from them, and
c the graph's first run is owed at the first root visit, before any decision; the option lets
c it run with three width-2 clauses rather than fifty, and BVE would refute the instance itself.
c The first width-2 clause, -3 -2+4, is rewritten by the unit x2 = 1 before the run, so the graph
c cites a rewritten clause, and x1 is unused, so its lines are renumbered back to the file's
c variables.
c The eight remaining clauses are every sign pattern over x6, x7, x8 with x3 added to each,
c so once x3 = 0 is substituted only search refutes them.
p xnf 8 12
2 0
-3 -2+4 0
-3 5 0
-3 4+5 0
3 6 7 8 0
3 6 7 -8 0
3 6 -7 8 0
3 6 -7 -8 0
3 -6 7 8 0
3 -6 7 -8 0
3 -6 -7 8 0
3 -6 -7 -8 0
